R NODULES  The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 25 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm fragment of fibrofatty breast tissue  with a firm fibrous area within the center  located 0 1cm from the tissue edge  The specimen is entirely frozen as FX 1 and is resubmitted in cassette A  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fragment of fibrofatty breast tissue  which is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm tan white firm stellate mass which grossly abuts multiple inked resection margins  Representative sections are submitted in B J  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name and unit number  in 2 parts  Labeled  right breast modified radical mastectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm right modified radical mastectomy specimen with an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm axillary tail  Overlying the specimen is a 16 x 6cm skin ellipse  that contains a REMOVED_DATE x 3 8cm nipple and areola  A 4 0cm long  linear  non healed  non sutured incision is present 3 0cm superolateral to the areola  Beneath this incision is a open  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm biopsy cavity  with a defect leading to the anterior surface of the specimen  located 0 9cm from the deep resection margin  and 7 0cm from the superior resection margin  The biopsy cavity is surrounded by focally firm  tan white and hemorrhagic parenchyma  and contains 2 sutures along its inferior edge  The remaining breast parenchyma is composed of lobulated  yellow  soft adipose tissue with interposed tan white  rubbery  fibrous tissue  The axillary tail is dissected to reveal multiple lymph nodes  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE   2 7cm in greatest dimension  Section Code  K  Biopsy cavity with deep resection margin  L O  Biopsy cavity with surrounding firm area  representative  P  Fibrous area  breast  representative  Q DD  Lymph nodes  Label  left modified radical mastectomy breast with axilla  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail  An REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm skin ellipse overlies the specimen  and contains a REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm nipple and areola  Sectioning reveals 4 discrete  tan white  scaly  gritty masses  The first is located in the lower outer quadrant  measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  and extends to 2 0cm of the deep  and 6 5cm of the inferior margin  