Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report  ML 10  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   CASE  ML 10  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME   Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient    Consulting Pathologist s   None  Assigned Resident Path  Anthony J Iafrate  M D   Ph D   Clinical History  Lung adenocarcinoma    Reports To   JOHN CHARLES WAIN  M D         FINAL DIAGNOSIS     TEST PERFORMED   ALK FISH ANALYSIS    INDICATION FOR TEST   Lung adenocarcinoma    FISH RESULTS     Fluorescence in situ hybridization of paraffin tumor tissue using a break apart  probe to the ALK gene revealed no rearrangement of the ALK locus     ISCN  REMOVED_CASE_ID  nomenclature  nuc ish  ALK x 2  47 50       INTERPRETATION     NORMAL  These results indicate NO ALK rearrangement in this case  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID       TEST INFORMATION   Rearrangement involving the ALK gene on 2p23 with the  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  gene on 2p21 is  present in approximately 5  of lung adenocarcinomas  Lung tumors with ALK  rearrangement have been shown to respond to ALK kinase inhibitors  1   In  addition  in 70 80  of ALK positive anaplastic large cell lymphomas  ALCL   ALK  is paired with Nucleophosmin  NPM  on 5q35  and with a variety of other genes  in the remaining  ALK rearrangements have also been described in other tumors  including inflammatory myofibroblastic tumors  neural tumors  and in some  subtypes of breast cancer and of rhabdomyosarcomas  Almost invariably  ALK  translocations result in chimeric proteins containing a 5  end partner fused to  the ALK tyrosine kinase domain at the 3  end  Deregulated ALK activity has an  oncogenic effect  and targeted therapies against this kinase are currently  being analyzed to treat cancers harboring rearrangements in the ALK locus   Fluorescence in situ hybridization  FISH  using formalin fixed  paraffin embedded specimens has been shown to be an effective method for  determining presence of these translocations  Briefly  5 micron sections of  formalin fixed paraffin embedded tumor material were prepared and an H E  section reviewed to select regions for hybridization that contain a majority of  tumor cells  An ALK break apart probe  Vysis LSI ALK  2p23  Dual Color  Break  Apart Rearrangement Probe  was hybridized  and used to calculate the number of  cells out of 50 scored containing a rearrangement  An ALK rearrangement is  reported if more than 15  of cells show split signals  CPT codes for this test    REMOVED_CASE_ID   morphometric analysis  in situ hybridization  each probe  manual  x 2      1  Kwak EL  Bang Y  Camidge DR  Shaw A  Solomon B  Maki RG  Ou SI  Dezube BJ   Janne PA  Costa DB  Varella Garcia M  Kim W  Lynch TJ  Fidias P  Stubbs H   Engelman JA  Sequist LV  Tan W  Gandhi L  Mino Kenudson M  Wei GC  Shreeve SM   Ratain MJ  Settleman J  Christensen JG  Haber DA  Wilner K  Salgia R  Shapiro  GI  Clark JW  Iafrate AJ  Anaplastic Lymphoma Kinase Inhibition in  Non Small Cell Lung Cancer  N Engl J Med  REMOVED_CASE_ID      This test was developed  and its performance characteristics were determined by  the MGH Diagnostic Molecular Pathology Laboratory  It has not been cleared or  approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  The FDA has determined that  such clearance or approval is not necessary  This test is used for clinical  purposes  Pursuant to the requirements of CLIA 88  this laboratory has  established and verified the test accuracy and precision     Questions concerning these values should be addressed to Dr  A  John Iafrate at   617  REMOVED_DATE MGH internal address  Diagnostic Molecular Pathology  Laboratory  Massachusetts General Hospital  55 Fruit St   Warren 508  Boston   MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID      Final Diagnosis by Anthony J Iafrate M D   Ph D   Electronically signed on  Monday REMOVED_MONTH 06   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 06 26 08PM  By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final  Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed  or corrected the diagnoses     PART   Fixed Tissue Block  MS 10  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   C   ALK FISH       report_end  , Yes.
