ody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 30     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  left breast lumpectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 3cm piece of fiberadipose tissue with attached REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm skin ellipse  The specimen is inked as follows  medial blue  superioral green  lateral red  inferior yellow  deep black  A representative section of the closest resection margin  deep  is frozen as FX 1  now in A  A representative section of the mass is frozen as FX 2  which was saved for further studies on Cox 5  The hard  pink white mass is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm in greatest dimension and is 0 7cm deep to the skin  The mass is surrounded by fibrous tissue  some of which extends to the deep margin of resection  The rest of the specimen is unremarkable  Section code  B E representative sections of breast mass F G fibrous tissue on either side of mass H  lateral and superior margins of specimen Labeled  left axillary nodes  is a REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm piece of grossly unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  Eleven lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 2cm in greatest dimension are submitted in I L  Resident  STUART HOUSER  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  DEEP MARGIN  IN SITU CARCINOMA PRESENT APPROXIMATELY 1MM FROM DEEP MARGIN  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  TUMOR  LEFT BREAST   INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  SAVE TO COX 5  O R  Resident  Ross C  Wheeler  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE U