Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 11 28 CLINICAL DATA  History of sister with breast cancer  Mammogram this year demonstrates a new density in the axillary tail of the left breast  Fine needle aspiration shows atypical clusters of papillary cells suspicious for intraductal carcinoma   REMOVED_CASE_ID  left breast biopsy showed benign pathology  On physical exam there is no palpable breast masses and no enlarged supraclavicular or axillary lymph nodes                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  95   INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA   5  FOCAL CHRONIC INFLAMMATION  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor measures 1 0cm in greatest dimension and involves the inked margin  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 41                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 09 49 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass   is a mass of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  It is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm white tan scirrhous nodule with irregular borders that abuts the inked margins  Representative sections frozen as FX 1 and saved frozen  The remainder submitted in A through E  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BREAST  BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  EDWIN S  MONUKI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  David William Rattner  M D  Paul Jerome Laraia  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , No.
